# Logging format (traceId + spanId)

Use this console layout everywhere. Do not invent a different pattern, logger-name field, or MDC key names.

## Expected line shape

```text
yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.SSS  LEVEL traceId  spanId - message
```

Example:

```text
2026-11-08 14:44:17.615  TRACE 6af0598884bbdcff38d1f7601c397a50  6152133d646b6078 - Completed 200 OK, headers={masked}
```

Field order (fixed):

1. Timestamp — `yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.SSS`
2. Level — left-padded to 5 (`%-5level`)
3. `traceId` then `spanId` from MDC (`%X{traceId}`, `%X{spanId}`)
4. Message — `%msg` (no logger name, no thread name)

## Dependencies (Maven)

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-micrometer-tracing-brave</artifactId>
</dependency>
<dependency>
    <groupId>io.micrometer</groupId>
    <artifactId>micrometer-tracing-bridge-brave</artifactId>
</dependency>
```

## Configuration

YAML:

```yaml
logging:
  pattern:
    console: '%clr(%d{yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.SSS}){cyan}  %clr(%-5level) %clr(%X{traceId}  %X{spanId}){magenta} - %msg%n'

management:
  tracing:
    sampling:
      probability: 1.0
```

Properties equivalent:

```properties
logging.pattern.console=%clr(%d{yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.SSS}){cyan}  %clr(%-5level) %clr(%X{traceId}  %X{spanId}){magenta} - %msg%n
management.tracing.sampling.probability=1.0
```

## Rules

- Always use MDC keys `traceId` and `spanId` (Brave / Micrometer defaults). Never rename them.
- Keep the exact spacing: two spaces after the timestamp, one space after level, two spaces between traceId and spanId, then ` - `.
- Prefer `%clr(...)` colors as above for local/dev consoles; keep the same tokens if a non-colored pattern is required.
- Sampling `1.0` is the default for environments that must always emit IDs; lower it only when explicitly requested for production load.
